{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact register packet head f994119557a1f3da5137341f721fb10cd9477a50 on builder/failed-claim-register-packet-20261105, tree 8555ec8a, for request c448c870 under promise f9db5e9e and review request 3466b012. Deploying this packet as written would cut off Git hosting for the 13 existing dap-demo rooms. I found this by reading the code at main 28839920; no run shows it.\n\nRequired:\n\n1. The install and offer stages move ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope from the Register 17 root sc_b5q435os… to the new Register 26 scope. The Artifacts adapter binds host authority to that one scope. artifactsOutside (packages/scope/src/artifacts-wiring.ts:117) calls hostBound(given, config.registerScope, host, namespace). For a destination, hostBound requires destinationBirth(given, registerScope), which refuses unless the destination's claim is at that exact register (host-wiring.ts:27). INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES reaches child admission, the health check and the scope index, but not hostBound. So after the switch, every destination born under Register 17 fails `bound`. Its read-token mints, publication sends, snapshots, credential reads and replies all return null or refuse. In practice, `dap clone`, publication and the MCP View diff stop working in all 13 rooms, while their status reads still succeed. The same holds for any pending Register 17 claim, whose repository creation also needs the register's binding. GitHub wiring has the same single-scope call (github-wiring.ts:122). The rollback stage would then strand Register 26 rooms in the same way.\n2. The procedure cannot detect this fault. It checks health, old-room reads and one child birth under the retained root. Each of those passes, while every Git operation in the old rooms fails. Add an old-room Git check after the switch: a read-token clone or publication in an existing demo room, before the scratch room.\n3. docs/deploy.md deletes a warning that is still true. The old text says a cutover on one Worker \"strands the old rooms, because each room's host authority names the old register\". The new text says that retaining the old roots in INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES is enough. At 28839920, it covers child creation but not host authority. Restore the warning, or change it once source supports host binding for every installed register.\n\nThe fix needs either a source change or a different plan, and that choice belongs to the planner. One source option makes host binding accept a destination or register born under any root in INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES. New creation would still use the current REGISTER_SCOPE. That change needs a witness: an old-root destination mints a read token after the switch, and a root outside the list stays refused. The other option is the separate Worker that docs/deploy.md recommended before this head.\n\nWhat holds, apart from this:\n\n- Scope: main 28839920 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head adds three commits, the branch is pushed, and the commit-message check passes for all three. It changes no production source, test, dependency or live Wrangler file. After gate commit 62faea13, only the note, the procedure and the gate manifest change.\n- The packet keeps the old root. The install, offer and rollback templates all list the Register 17 root in INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES, as planner ruling ef31035a and finding 72d96e46 require for child creation. The rollback restores the old REGISTER_SCOPE, Artifacts scope and Register 17 offer.\n- The gate passed. gate.exit reads exit 0 at 62faea13: Node 135, Counting 56, Plain 3,925 with one skip and Native 1,103 with two skips. before.json records a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43.\n- Evidence: both manifests match the SHA-256 values in the note. Their 31 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, both SHA256SUMS files match, and the credential scan finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: blocking finding. A one-Worker cutover needs host authority for every installed register, not only child admission. Either the packet waits for that source change, or Register 26 goes on its own Worker.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The fault denies service; it widens no authority.\n\nSimplification: no required change beyond the above.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e7eedf6a79d8bfc519a54a2720368da650c1918d","binding":"assigned","head":"f994119557a1f3da5137341f721fb10cd9477a50","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:65a42309bdce6741640d11b54aa9768f567bb94a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f9db5e9e73a857f4a34eb4de468a0ca402406d6e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:65a42309bdce6741640d11b54aa9768f567bb94a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}